Dispatch you got yesterday (orchestrator): issue #6229 fix(control-surface): a Launchkey's transport buttons do nothing after the device is unplugged and replugged. Lane fix/control-surface-reconnect. Paths src/modules/ControlSurface/useCases/ and its __tests__/. Acceptance: after a disconnect/connect statechange for the same port id, transport CCs from the surface reach Play/Stop/Record again; no duplicate handlers on the old port. Deliver through pnpm deliver once review is accepted and checks are green.

you (yesterday): Opened #6231 fix(control-surface): rebind a surface's input when its port reconnects (closes #6229). Cause: bindSurfaceInputs attaches onmidimessage once at discovery; on replug Web MIDI hands back a new MIDIInput object for the same id, so the handler stays on the dead one. Fix: rebind on statechange 'connected' and detach from the previous input. Review round 1 accepted with no findings. Waiting on CI.

